From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:41:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] netprofm: Keep networks as profiles, connections as the
 interfaces up, and tell sinks what changes.

As on Windows 11 a network is a profile in the registry, known by its
gateway and kept whether connected or not, named Network, Network 2 and
so on; an interface without a gateway is an unidentified network of its
own.  A connection is an interface that is up, with an id of its own
and the interface's as its adapter id, and reaches the internet through
a gateway, its subnet without one, and nothing with only link-local
addresses.  The host's changes of addresses, interfaces and routes
refresh the state and the sinks, called through the global interface
table in their own apartments, are told what changed; the network list
interfaces get proxies, and IDispatch works through the type library.
The connection points enumerate in Windows' order, with the connection
cost events among them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

